Subject: Use the named minimatch export in the resource filter
Origin: DHI-internal (UI dependency compatibility)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/argoproj/argo-cd.git 94037c4d4e1af4bd0651d37a179fbd9e347e668c
Verify: cmd `pnpm build` expect "compiled"
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI overrides the upstream minimatch dependency)
Drop-When: never: required while upstream uses callable namespace imports with the DHI minimatch override

The DHI minimatch override exports an object containing a named minimatch
function. Argo CD 3.6 also uses minimatch in its resource filter, where a namespace
import remains an object and throws when a wildcard filter is evaluated.
Use the named function while retaining the dependency override.

--- a/ui/src/app/resources/components/resources-list/resources-filter.tsx
+++ b/ui/src/app/resources/components/resources-list/resources-filter.tsx
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 import {useData} from 'argo-ui/v2';
-import * as minimatch from 'minimatch';
+import {minimatch} from 'minimatch';
 import * as React from 'react';
